{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_56","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Implementation notes: Interlock EX-forwarded MUL operands\n\nWhat changed:\n- Factored rtl/alu.sv into simple_alu and mul_unit helper modules while keeping the legacy alu module and its simple_out/mul_out/out ports for standalone tests.\n- Updated rtl/ex_stage.sv so normal ALU, branch, address, store-data, and DIV/REM operands still use the existing EX/MEM and MEM/WB forwarding muxes.\n- Added a dedicated multiply operand mux in EX that only selects ID/EX register values or MEM/WB writeback data. It never selects the EX/MEM forwarded-result rail.\n- Updated MUL RVFI source-value propagation so retiring MUL/MULH/MULHSU/MULHU instructions report the operands actually used by the multiplier.\n- Added MEM/WB-only multiply forwarding selects in rtl/forward_unit.sv so the multiplier input mux does not depend on the EX/MEM producer compare.\n- Added a MUL-specific adjacent-producer interlock in rtl/hazard_unit.sv, wired from rtl/core.sv. If IF/ID is a MUL-family instruction and current ID/EX will write a non-load result to a matching source register, the pipeline injects one bubble with the same dmem-stall and ex_busy priority as load-use.\n\nDeviations:\n- Loads are still handled by the existing load-use hazard rather than the new MUL-specific producer predicate, since load results are not EX/MEM-forwardable in this core.\n- I did not add a new cocotb test file; the RTL behavior was checked with lint, riscv-formal, and cosim within the wall-clock budget.\n- I did not run make timing.\n\nConcerns:\n- The top-level Makefile invokes test/cosim/build.sh with its default NRET=2, but cores/bench/core.yaml declares nret: 1 and the core exposes only channel 0. The bare `make cosim TARGET=bench` therefore fails during C++ compile before simulation by looking for `_1` RVFI ports. Running `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` exercises the actual bench core contract and passes.\n\nLocal verification:\n- PASS: `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`\n- PASS: `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh` (53 passed, 0 failed)\n- PASS: `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` (2 ELFs tested)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"agent_message","text":"Done.\n\nImplemented the MUL adjacent-producer interlock and split the multiplier operand path so it uses only ID/EX or MEM/WB data, with EX/MEM forwarding preserved for non-MUL consumers.\n\nVerification:\n- `verilator --lint-only ...`: pass\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass, 53/53\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, 2 ELFs\n\nNote: bare `make cosim TARGET=bench` still defaults to `NRET=2` and fails before simulation for this nret=1 core; documented in `cores/bench/implementation_notes.md`."}}
