{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"The formal wrapper drives zero-wait dmem, so the new logic has to preserve byte-exact RVFI even when the external bus is silent on a hit. The main extra care point is making cached-hit `mem_rdata` report the cached raw word, not whatever happens to be on `io_dmemRData`."}}
