{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"agent_message","text":"I’m adding the stale-store guard right in the probe path: while a store for a RAM line is in MEM, a younger EX load to that same line is forced to miss, then refetches after the store completes. That costs a repeat load in a rare case but protects correctness under dmem stalls."}}
