{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"## Move multiply onto the MEM-stage rail\n\nChanged the core datapath so EX no longer instantiates or latches the\ncombinational multiply product. EX now computes only the simple ALU rail,\nclassifies MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU as `WB_SEL_MUL`, and carries the already\nforwarded `rs1_val` / `rs2_val` into EX/MEM. MEM computes the exact multiply\nvariant from those registered operands, including the `RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS`\nsubstitutes, and latches the value into the existing MEM/WB `mul_result` rail.\n\nForwarding now suppresses EX/MEM advertising for `WB_SEL_MUL`, since the value\nis not available until MEM/WB. The hazard unit extends the existing load-use\nbubble to ID/EX multiply producers, so only an immediately following dependent\ninstruction stalls for one cycle. Back-to-back independent multiplies can still\nissue one per cycle.\n\nAdded `test/test_mul_mem_stage.py` for independent consecutive multiplies,\nadjacent MUL-use stall/forwarding, high-half signed/unsigned variants, and\nMEM/WB forwarding with a one-instruction gap.\n\nNo intentional deviations from the hypothesis. One caveat: the hazard unit\nkeeps the prior conservative source-field compare style, so OP-IMM immediates\nwhose bits look like `rs2` may still create the same kind of false dependency\nthe old load-use logic already had.\n\nLocal checks:\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`: pass\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_mul_mem_stage.py`: pass\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, 2 ELFs tested\n\nThe bare `make cosim TARGET=bench` command in this checkout defaults the C++\nharness to `NRET=2` and fails to compile against this core's `nret: 1` port\nset; rerunning with `NRET=1` matches `cores/bench/core.yaml` and passes.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented the MEM-stage multiply move.\n\nChanged:\n- EX no longer computes/latches multiply products.\n- MEM computes `MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU` from registered EX/MEM operands.\n- EX/MEM forwarding no longer advertises unavailable multiply results.\n- Hazard logic now gives immediate multiply consumers a load-like one-cycle bubble.\n- Added `cores/bench/test/test_mul_mem_stage.py`.\n- Wrote `cores/bench/implementation_notes.md`.\n\nChecks:\n- Verilator lint: pass\n- Formal: pass, `53 passed, 0 failed`\n- Targeted cocotb multiply test: pass\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, 2 ELFs tested\n\nNote: bare `make cosim TARGET=bench` defaulted the harness to `NRET=2` and failed looking for `_1` RVFI ports; rerunning with `NRET=1` matches `cores/bench/core.yaml`."}}
