{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"ls -l cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"-rw-rw----+ 1 hwebench3 hwebench3 1786 Oct  4 10:34 cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\nRegistered static-not-taken repair implementation notes\n\nWhat changed:\n- `if_stage.sv` now treats `pc + 4` as the normal static not-taken next PC and only redirects from a registered `repair`/`repair_target` input.\n- `ex_stage.sv` now emits `repair_req`/`repair_target` when the resolved next PC differs from `pc + 4`. It also accepts `kill`, which gates valid EX work, suppresses divider start/busy for wrong-path DIV/REM, and bubbles EX/MEM.\n- `core.sv` adds the repair target/token flops. EX repair is captured only when EX/MEM is not held by a dmem stall, then the following cycle redirects IF and kills the captured fall-through instruction.\n- `hazard_unit.sv` uses the registered repair token to flush ID/EX for the second fall-through instruction and to suppress load-use stalls from a wrong-path load.\n\nDeviations:\n- I did not add a kill bit to `core_pkg.sv`; a single top-level registered token is enough for this pipeline because IF/ID is combinational and ID/EX is the only wrong-path instruction that can reach EX.\n- I left the existing branch/jump RVFI `pc_next` computation in EX so retired control-flow instructions still report their architectural target.\n\nConcerns:\n- Taken branches and jumps now pay the intended extra cycle. No dynamic predictor, BTB, IF decode, or IF/ID target metadata was added.\n- Local `make cosim TARGET=bench` invokes the harness with its default `NRET=2`, which mismatches this core's `nret: 1` port set. Rerunning as `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` matches `core.yaml` and passes.\n\nLocal status:\n- Verilator lint: pass\n- Cocotb focused branch redirect: pass\n- Cocotb pipeline: pass\n- Formal: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed with `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`\n- Cosim: pass with `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
