{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"test -f cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,200p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"## Hot Loop Replay Predictor\n\nImplemented a single 16-word hot-loop replay store in `if_stage.sv`. EX trains it on taken backward conditional branches, IF fills entries from normal ready imem fetches, and a later fetch at the learned loop start serves instructions locally with an effective imem-ready hit. The hazard unit now sees that effective ready signal through `core.sv`, so replayed instructions do not bubble when raw `io_imemReady` is low.\n\nPipeline metadata additions are limited to compact replay state in `if_id_t`/`id_ex_t`: replay hit, 4-bit loop index, and predicted-wrap. EX suppresses a predicted backedge redirect only after resolving a taken branch whose target matches `pc - loop_idx*4`; otherwise it repairs to the resolved target or `pc+4` and IF cancels replay on the redirect.\n\nDeviation: the replay window is fixed at 16 words and one entry. Longer backward branches invalidate the learned entry rather than partially replaying.\n\nConcern: the IF local array adds a dynamic instruction mux and small valid-mask logic to fetch. It should recover imem stall cycles inside tight loops, but timing benefit depends on whether that mux is cheaper than the avoided bubbles for CoreMark's actual hot loops.\n\nLocal checks:\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`: pass\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass on attempt 2. Attempt 1 failed `pc_fwd_ch0`; fixed by validating predicted wrap target in EX and repairing symbolic instruction changes.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench`: local build used `NRET=2` and failed to compile against this `nret: 1` core's single-channel RVFI ports.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, selftest and CoreMark.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented the hot-loop replay predictor in `cores/bench/rtl`.\n\nChanged:\n- Added 16-word IF-stage loop replay store and effective imem-ready hit path.\n- Added compact replay metadata through IF/ID and ID/EX.\n- Added EX training for taken backward branches.\n- Added predicted-wrap validation/repair in EX so loop exits and symbolic instruction changes recover correctly.\n- Wired `imem_ready_eff` into the hazard unit path via `core.sv`.\n- Wrote `cores/bench/implementation_notes.md`.\n\nChecks:\n- Verilator lint: pass\n- Formal: pass on attempt 2, `53 passed, 0 failed`\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, selftest and CoreMark\n\nNote: plain `make cosim TARGET=bench` locally compiled the harness as `NRET=2` and failed looking for channel-1 RVFI ports on this `nret: 1` core, so I reran with `NRET=1`."}}
