{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"test -f cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"WB zero-hit predictor implementation notes\n\nWhat changed:\n- Removed the same-cycle write-first data bypass from rtl/reg_file.sv. Reads now select only x0 or the stored register array.\n- Added a WB-to-ID interlock in rtl/hazard_unit.sv. When IF/ID rs1 or rs2 matches the valid WB destination, the core holds fetch and bubbles ID/EX for one cycle so decode rereads the just-written register value.\n- Wired WB write-enable and destination from rtl/core.sv into the hazard unit.\n- Updated the regfile unit test to expect stored data during a same-cycle write/read, then the new value after the write edge.\n- Added test_wb_zero_hit_predictor.py for distance-three producer/consumer hits, x0 immunity, no-hit decode spacing, bus-stall overlap, and redirect priority.\n\nDeviations:\n- The interlock compares the raw IF/ID rs1 and rs2 fields, matching the existing register-file read ports and preserving the current RVFI source-data convention. It may bubble on unused raw fields, but avoids adding another decode-use classifier on the hazard path.\n\nConcerns:\n- The predictor trades a rare decode bubble for a shorter regfile read mux. False hits from unused instruction fields are possible because the compare is intentionally raw-field based.\n\nLocal verification:\n- Verilator lint passed:\n  verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv\n- Focused cocotb tests passed:\n  pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py cores/bench/test/test_wb_zero_hit_predictor.py\n- Full bench cocotb unit suite passed:\n  pytest -q cores/bench/test\n- Formal passed, 53 passed / 0 failed:\n  RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh\n- Cosim passed for selftest and CoreMark:\n  NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench\n\nNotes on local commands:\n- The bare formal command exits in this checkout unless RTL_DIR and CORE_NAME are set.\n- The bare make cosim invocation builds the C++ harness with its default NRET=2; passing NRET=1 matches cores/bench/core.yaml.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
