{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Decode-stage backward branch predictor\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `id_ex_t.predicted_taken` so conditional branches carry only the one-bit decode prediction into EX.\n- `id_stage.sv` now recognizes valid conditional branches with negative immediates, computes `pc + imm`, and emits a predicted redirect for word-aligned targets.\n- `if_stage.sv` accepts the decode redirect with lower priority than EX redirects and only while the frontend is not stalled.\n- `ex_stage.sv` suppresses the normal taken-branch redirect when a predicted backward branch is actually taken, and redirects to `pc + 4` when the prediction is wrong.\n- `core.sv` wires the decode prediction request and target between ID and IF.\n\n## Deviations\n\n- The predictor filters out misaligned branch targets in ID. EX still handles misaligned branch traps for all branches; the filter avoids fetching down a target path that EX would later suppress as a trap.\n- I did not add a new test file. The implementation was checked through lint, formal, and cosim instead.\n\n## Concerns\n\n- The decode `pc + imm` adder is now on the ID-to-PC control path. This matches the hypothesis, but it is still a frontend timing path to watch in Gowin timing.\n- Branches that are load-use dependent are not predicted while stalled; this preserves operand correctness and gives up the predictor win for that dependency case.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- PASS: `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`\n- PASS: `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`\n- PASS: `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`\n- Note: plain `make cosim TARGET=bench` failed because this Makefile defaults the C++ harness to `NRET=2`, while `cores/bench/core.yaml` declares `nret: 1`; rerunning with `NRET=1` matches the core contract.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
