{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r1s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-003-r1s2\ntitle: \"Tiny BTB next-PC predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current five-stage core fetches the sequential PC until a branch or jump\n  resolves in EX, so every taken conditional branch and every jump pays a\n  front-end flush penalty. CoreMark's timed region has hot loops, direct calls,\n  and repeated returns, making taken-control penalties a plausible IPC loss that\n  can be attacked without touching the ALU critical path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a small direct-mapped next-PC predictor in IF: a 16-entry BTB indexed by\n  fetch PC, with a modest tag, predicted target, and 2-bit taken counter. IF\n  uses a valid tag hit with a taken counter to fetch the predicted target;\n  otherwise it fetches PC+4. EX computes the architectural next PC exactly as\n  today, compares it with the predicted next PC carried down the pipe, and only\n  redirects/flushes on a mismatch. Update the BTB in EX for conditional\n  branches, JAL, and JALR; train conditional counters up/down and force jumps\n  strongly taken. This should remove most recurring loop and call/return\n  redirects while adding only a small PC-indexed lookup outside the current\n  forwarding-to-ALU worst path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Extend IF/ID, ID/EX, and EX/MEM payloads with predicted next-PC metadata used for redirect verification and RVFI-safe propagation.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add the 16-entry BTB/counter predictor, drive predicted next PC into the PC update path, and expose prediction metadata to decode.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare resolved architectural next PC against the carried predicted next PC, redirect only on mismatch, and emit BTB update information.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire predictor metadata and update signals between IF and EX while keeping the existing single-retire RVFI contract unchanged.\"\n  - file: test/test_branch_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add focused cocotb coverage for correct execution through predicted taken branches, not-taken retraining, jumps, returns, and mispredict recovery.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
