{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r4s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-003-r4s2\ntitle: \"Single-entry learned loop predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts show that CoreMark does have recoverable loop\n  redirect bubbles: the two-entry learned loop-target predictor reduced the\n  timed cycle count by roughly five percent. Its score still missed the\n  acceptance bar because the extra entry comparisons, target muxing, and\n  predictor plumbing cost about four percent of Fmax. The most promising\n  predictor angle is therefore not a richer predictor, but a smaller one that\n  preserves the dominant loop benefit while giving timing back.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the two-entry learned loop-target idea with a single exact-entry\n  backward-branch predictor. Train the lone entry only from resolved taken\n  backward conditional branches in EX, storing the branch PC and resolved\n  target. IF performs one PC equality check and one target mux, with no\n  instruction decode, no immediate adder, no counters, and no associative\n  two-entry priority logic. Carry only a predicted-loop-hit bit down the pipe;\n  EX already computes the architectural next PC and redirects only when the\n  prediction disagrees with the actual branch outcome. CoreMark's hottest\n  loop back edge should keep most of the previous cycle-count win, while the\n  smaller predictor should recover enough Fmax to clear the champion margin.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add one predicted-loop-hit metadata bit to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles for EX-stage validation.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a single-entry exact PC/target loop predictor lookup with no IF instruction decode or target adder.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Train the single predictor entry from resolved taken backward branches and redirect on predicted-versus-actual mismatch.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the predictor hit metadata and EX-stage update signals without changing the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_single_loop_predictor.py\n    description: \"Cover cold misses, repeated backward branch hits, loop exits, and recovery across imem and dmem stalls.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
