{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r10s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-001-r10s0\ntitle: \"Ungated hot execute result rails\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion is limited by the forwarded execute operand path into the\n  EX/MEM multiply-result rail.  Prior attempts show that making MUL multi-cycle,\n  changing multiplier decomposition, or adding predictor feedback tends to lose\n  more CoreMark fitness than it saves.  The remaining timing opportunity is to\n  remove avoidable control muxing around the hot registered result rails while\n  preserving the existing single-cycle multiply throughput and memory behavior.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split the EX/MEM and MEM/WB pipeline registers so side-effect metadata\n  (valid, control, rd, memory address/data metadata, and RVFI-retired fields)\n  keeps the existing hold/clear semantics, but hot arithmetic result rails such\n  as simple_result, mul_result, div_result, and jump_result update through\n  true ungated data flops whenever their value is architecturally ignored.\n\n  In particular, do not drive reset, divider-bubble, redirect-bubble, or dmem\n  hold muxes into the mul_result/simple_result D paths.  During invalid bubbles\n  or held memory operations these rails may contain don't-care values because\n  valid/wb_sel/reg_write/mem_to_reg already prevent retirement, register writes,\n  memory requests, and forwarding from observing them.  This should remove one\n  or more LUT/enable layers from the current multiply-result setup path without\n  changing IPC, top-level IO, RVFI order, or the RV32IM arithmetic contract.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Split EX/MEM register updates so hot result rails update ungated while only valid/control and memory-observable fields keep reset, divider-bubble, and dmem-hold semantics.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Mirror the split-register style at MEM/WB where safe, keeping forwarding-critical load data and RVFI memory metadata stable during dmem holds while avoiding unnecessary muxing on ignored arithmetic rails.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Apply the same side-effect-control versus don't-care-data distinction to ID/EX bubbles so reset and redirect/load-use flushes do not fan out into wide unused data fields.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline_bubbles.py\n    description: \"Cover redirects, load-use bubbles, divider bubbles, and dmem stalls to prove stale or changing don't-care rails cannot retire, write registers, issue memory operations, or corrupt RVFI-visible state.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
