{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_15", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor r in [json.loads(l) for l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines() if l.strip()]:\n    if r['id'] in {'hyp-20261004-002-r4s1','hyp-20261004-002-r5s1'}:\n        print('---', r['id'])\n        print('title:', r['title'])\n        print('hypothesis:', r.get('hypothesis'))\n        print('notes:', r.get('implementation_notes'))\n        print('critical_path:', r.get('critical_path'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "--- hyp-20261004-002-r4s1\ntitle: Split execute AGU from ALU result rail\nhypothesis: {'motivation': \"The current champion's remaining worst path is reported through ID, EX, the\\nALU, and into the data-memory side of the design. Prior structural attempts\\nthat added front-end buffering or deeper IF/ID state lost more Fmax and\\ncontrol simplicity than they recovered, while making MUL multicycle hurt\\nCoreMark IPC. A narrower structural target is the load/store effective\\naddress path itself: memory operations only need rs1+imm for dmem address,\\nmasks, alignment, and RVFI memory metadata, but today that value is carried\\nthrough the same general ALU result rail and muxing used by shifts, compares,\\njumps, and single-cycle multiply results.\\n\", 'hypothesis': 'Add a dedicated execute-stage address-generation rail for LOAD and STORE\\ninstructions. Compute effective_addr = forwarded_rs1 + imm beside the\\nnormal ALU, latch it in EX/MEM, and have MEM use that field for dmem_addr,\\nbyte-lane masks, misalignment checks, load extraction, and RVFI mem_addr.\\nKeep the existing ALU rail for arithmetic writeback and keep MUL single-cycle;\\nDIV/REM remain on the current iterative path. This should let the timed\\ndmem-address path bypass the full ALU result case tree and multiplier result\\nmuxing without adding CoreMark cycles, while preserving exact memory semantics\\nand the nret=1 RVFI contract.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 6, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'description': 'Add an effective-address field to the EX/MEM payload so memory address metadata no longer has to share the general ALU result rail.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Compute forwarded_rs1+imm in a dedicated AGU path for loads/stores, latch it into EX/MEM, and leave the existing ALU path for arithmetic, jumps, and single-cycle MUL.'}, {'file': 'rtl/mem_stage.sv', 'description': 'Use the EX/MEM effective-address field for dmem_addr, byte masks, misalignment detection, load shifting, and RVFI aligned \n…[2390 of 5462 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:617ad2322ac502b5]…\nription': 'Latch op-class result rails independently, remove the pre-register result_to_mem/jump/div mux from the critical alu_result input, and expose a registered forwarding result selected from those rails.'}, {'file': 'rtl/mem_stage.sv', 'description': 'Propagate the split result rails and writeback-select metadata through MEM/WB without disturbing the dedicated effective_addr memory path.'}, {'file': 'rtl/wb_stage.sv', 'description': 'Select the architectural writeback value from registered result rails or load data in WB, and feed the same value to RVFI rd_wdata.'}, {'file': 'test/test_execute_result_rails.py', 'description': 'Cover ALU, MUL variants, DIV/REM completion, JAL/JALR link results, dependent forwarding, and load writeback after the result-rail split.'}]}\nnotes: \ncritical_path: {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.mul_result_8_s0', 'slack_ns': -10.845, 'arrival_ns': 21.14, 'logic_cells': 9, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
