{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r1s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-001-r1s0\ntitle: \"Gate M-extension arithmetic off the ALU fast path\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The only recorded timing result has a very deep worst path running from the\n  pipeline registers through the forwarding muxes and into the execute ALU.\n  The current combinational ALU unconditionally builds multiplier partial\n  products and exposes divider/remainder operators in the same wide result mux\n  used by common CoreMark integer ops, which is a poor fit for the FPGA and\n  likely dominates Fmax even when the retiring instruction is ADD, branch, or\n  load/store address generation.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split the execute ALU into a narrow RV32I fast path and an M-extension slow\n  path selected only when funct7 marks an M instruction. Keep the visible\n  pipeline contract intact, but gate the multiplier/divider operands to zero\n  unless the operation is MUL/DIV/REM and restructure the ALU case so ADD/SUB,\n  compares, shifts, boolean ops, branch targets, and memory addresses do not\n  traverse the synthesized M-unit result mux. This should reduce the critical\n  path for the overwhelmingly common CoreMark instructions while preserving\n  exact RV32M results for the relatively rare M ops.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Refactor the combinational ALU into RV32I fast-path logic plus operand-gated M-extension logic, with the final mux arranged so non-M operations avoid multiplier/divider fan-in.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Optionally add compact ALU operation classification constants or helper encodings if needed to make M-op detection cheap and local.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Optionally pass an is_m_op-style qualifier or otherwise keep M-extension selection local to execute without changing pipeline depth or top-level IO.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Extend or rerun ALU unit vectors around all MUL/DIV/REM edge cases to guard the gated M-extension datapath.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
