{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r1s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-001-r1s0\ntitle: \"Move DIV/REM off the single-cycle ALU path\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The only recorded timing result has a very deep worst path running from the\n  pipeline registers through the forwarding muxes and into the execute ALU.\n  The current RV32M ALU implements DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU with single-cycle\n  SystemVerilog \"/\" and \"%\" operators, forcing Gowin timing to close a full\n  32-bit divider/remainder path in one cycle even though CoreMark's timed loop\n  is dominated by loads, stores, branches, simple integer ops, and MUL.\nhypothesis: |\n  Keep the RV32I ALU and MUL/MULH variants single-cycle, but replace the\n  combinational DIV/REM cases with a small iterative divide unit in execute.\n  When a DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU enters EX, freeze upstream pipeline state until the\n  quotient/remainder is ready, then let the instruction advance normally with\n  the exact RV32M result and RVFI metadata. This removes the long divider and\n  modulo logic from the cycle-time path scored by static timing, while the IPC\n  cost should be negligible for CoreMark if timed-region divides are rare.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 18\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Remove single-cycle DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operators from the combinational ALU and leave only RV32I plus single-cycle multiply results on the fast path.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate/control an iterative divider for DIV/REM ops, hold the EX/MEM register while it runs, and mux its completed result into the normal ALU result field.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Fold the divider-busy condition into the existing pipeline freeze logic so fetch/decode/execute state is held without double retirement or lost redirects.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Optionally add cheap ALU-op classification constants for DIV/REM detection and divider result selection.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Update or supplement M-extension vectors so divide-by-zero, signed overflow, signed remainder, and unsigned cases remain exact with the new multicycle datapath.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
