{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r7s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-001-r7s0\ntitle: \"Bypass ALU operand muxes for MUL\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion's worst path terminates at the EX/MEM mul_result rail\n  through u_ex/u_alu.  Recent attempts show that CoreMark needs single-cycle\n  MUL throughput, and that changing multiplier structure or adding multiply\n  bubbles loses more than it gains.  There is still a local timing tax on the\n  multiply path: the multiplier consumes the generic ALU operands after the\n  AUIPC rs1/pc mux and the rs2/immediate mux, even though all RV32M multiply\n  instructions are R-type and must use the forwarded rs1 and rs2 values.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split the ALU's simple-operation operands from its multiply operands.  Keep\n  the existing generic a/b inputs for ADD/SUB/logic/shift/SLT/AUIPC/LUI, but\n  feed the MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU product expressions from raw post-forward\n  rs1 and rs2 rails supplied by ex_stage.  The formal ALTOPS multiply stand-ins\n  should use the same direct multiply operands so cocotb, cosim, and formal\n  continue to agree.\n\n  This should remove two 32-bit operand-select muxes from the current\n  regfile/forwarding-to-DSP-to-EX/MEM setup path without changing pipeline\n  control, DSP count, result-rail selection, forwarding semantics, or CoreMark\n  cycle count.  It deliberately avoids the failed directions from the recent\n  log: no shared high-half correction after the DSP, no multicycle MUL sidecar,\n  and no front-end predictor metadata.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Add direct multiply operand inputs and compute MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU, including RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutes, from those inputs instead of the generic ALU a/b mux outputs.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Feed the ALU's multiply operand inputs with the already-forwarded rs1 and rs2 rails while leaving the existing generic alu_a/alu_b path for simple ALU, AUIPC, LUI, branches, and memory address work.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Update the standalone ALU cocotb wrapper/tests for the widened ALU interface and keep signedness edge vectors around all multiply variants.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
