{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-002-r12s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-002-r12s1\ntitle: \"Load-hit LSU data cache\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The accepted core still blocks the whole pipeline whenever a load or store in\n  MEM sees io_dmemReady low.  Recent history shows that timing-only execute\n  retiming is mostly exhausted, while the tiny I-cache experiment proved that\n  hiding the random memory stall stream can recover many CoreMark cycles even\n  after paying some extra logic.  The unexplored structural opportunity is on\n  the LSU side: CoreMark's 2K data set should have high temporal locality, and\n  load hits can be satisfied locally without touching the top-level memory RAM\n  or adding a posted-store arbiter.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny direct-mapped, word-granular load cache inside mem_stage for normal\n  RAM addresses only.  On a cacheable load hit, feed the cached 32-bit word into\n  the existing byte/halfword extraction path, assert an effective dmem-ready\n  signal to the hazard unit, and suppress the external read request so the\n  pipeline does not freeze when io_dmemReady is low.  On a load miss, preserve\n  the current blocking behavior and fill the line when io_dmemReady returns.\n\n  Stores, UART/MMIO, marker accesses, and misaligned accesses should remain\n  uncached and blocking; a store to a cached RAM line may invalidate or update\n  the line only after the external write completes.  This deliberately avoids\n  the prior posted-store mux that broke Gowin dmem inference, while targeting a\n  larger IPC gain than the I-cache because dmem stalls currently freeze the\n  entire backend.  The cache lookup is anchored in MEM from registered EX/MEM\n  address/control rails, so it should avoid the IF next-PC and redirect paths\n  that made previous structural front-end changes fragile.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a small direct-mapped RAM-address load cache, select cached read data on hits, fill on blocking load misses, and keep stores/MMIO/misaligned accesses on the existing uncached path.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Use an effective dmem-ready input from the LSU so cache-hit loads do not freeze IF/ID/EX/MEM even when raw io_dmemReady is low.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the mem_stage cache-hit/effective-ready signal into the hazard unit while preserving the top-level dmem and nret=1 RVFI contracts.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add minimal LSU/cache metadata constants or bundle fields if needed for cacheable RAM detection and RVFI-correct load data propagation.\"\n  - file: test/test_dcache.py\n    description: \"Cover load hits under dmem stalls, miss fill behavior, store invalidation or update, uncached MMIO/marker accesses, byte and halfword loads, redirects, and reset invalidation.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
