{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-002-r14s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-002-r14s1\ntitle: \"Register MEM/WB forward result\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion is still limited by the execute operand/forwarding path:\n  recent timing reports repeatedly show paths through the forwarding logic into\n  the EX ALU and EX/MEM register.  Prior successful work split the EX result\n  rails so the producer stage no longer pays a full result-select mux before\n  the EX/MEM boundary, but MEM/WB forwarding and regfile write-first reads still\n  consume a late combinational writeback mux every cycle.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a registered MEM/WB writeback-data rail that is selected in the MEM stage\n  from the already-registered EX/MEM result rails or the load extraction result.\n  Then make wb_stage, the regfile write port, RVFI rd_wdata, and the MEM/WB\n  bypass path consume that registered value directly instead of reselecting\n  simple/MUL/DIV/JAL/load data in the WB stage.\n\n  This preserves the accepted split EX/MEM result-rail structure, so it should\n  not reintroduce the harmful wide ALU/MUL/JAL mux on the EX/MEM setup path.\n  The new select happens one stage later, where all non-load inputs are already\n  pipeline-registered and load_data is already computed for MEM/WB.  The expected\n  benefit is a shorter WB-to-ID write-first path and a shorter MEM/WB-to-EX\n  bypass path, with no CoreMark IPC cost, no predictor metadata, and no change\n  to the nret=1 top-level/RVFI contract.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a wb_data field to the MEM/WB payload while keeping the existing result rails for RVFI/debug compatibility and low-risk routing.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Select the final writeback value from registered EX/MEM rails or load_data before the MEM/WB register, and retain it correctly across dmem holds.\"\n  - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n    description: \"Replace the late writeback data mux with the registered MEM/WB wb_data rail while preserving w_en and x0 behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Continue forwarding wb_w_data from WB to EX, now sourced from the registered wb_data rail, and keep RVFI rd_wdata aligned with the retired write.\"\n  - file: test/test_wb_forward_result.py\n    description: \"Add focused cocotb coverage for MEM/WB forwarding after ALU, MUL, DIV, JAL, and load results, including dmem stall holds.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
