{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-002-r2s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-002-r2s1\ntitle: \"Register the IF/ID boundary\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion's worst path no longer runs through the divider; it runs\n  from register-file state through ID/EX, EX redirect logic, the combinational\n  IF payload, hazard logic, and back into the ID/EX register. That loop exists\n  because if_stage emits a combinational IF/ID bundle and uses same-cycle\n  redirect/flush to rewrite the instruction to NOP before the hazard unit and\n  ID stage consume it. CoreMark now needs a structural timing cut in the\n  pipeline-control loop, not another arithmetic-unit change.\nhypothesis: |\n  Turn IF/ID into a real registered pipeline boundary with explicit valid,\n  enable, and kill behavior. Fetch should capture pc/instruction only when the\n  instruction bus is ready and the downstream stage can accept it, hold the\n  registered payload during dmem/divider/load-use stalls, and clear only the\n  valid bit on redirect or front-end bubble. The hazard unit should compare\n  load-use hazards against the registered IF/ID instruction and its valid bit\n  instead of a redirect-masked combinational instruction coming out of IF.\n  Redirect can still update the PC immediately and flush the two younger\n  instructions, but the EX-to-IF-to-hazard-to-ID same-cycle feedback path is\n  removed. The expected win is higher Fmax from a cleaner register-to-register\n  control boundary while preserving single-cycle MUL throughput and the current\n  single-retire RVFI contract.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 12\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Keep the existing IF/ID payload shape but treat it as a registered pipeline bundle with a meaningful valid bit; add fields only if the implementation needs separate fetch-ready metadata.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Replace the combinational IF/ID output with a registered fetch/decode boundary that holds on stalls, captures on imem ready, kills valid on redirect, and keeps PC redirect priority intact.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Base load-use detection on the registered IF/ID valid instruction and separate redirect kill from the load-use compare so redirect no longer feeds through the IF NOP mux into stall generation.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Consume the registered IF/ID bundle with explicit enable/kill semantics and avoid using redirect-masked combinational instruction bits for rs address capture.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the revised IF/ID enable, hold, and kill controls between IF, ID, and hazard while preserving the nret=1 top-level IO and RVFI behavior.\"\n  - file: test/test_if_id_boundary.py\n    description: \"Add focused cocotb coverage for redirect flushes, imem stalls, dmem stalls, and load-use bubbles across the new registered IF/ID boundary.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
