{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-002-r3s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-002-r3s1\ntitle: \"Add a tiny instruction prefetch FIFO\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion has already removed the divider from the hot execute\n  path and the remaining predictor-style front-end changes lost timing. The\n  benchmark still drives about 22% pseudo-random instruction-memory stalls,\n  and the current IF stage turns every one of those stalls into a front-end\n  bubble because it has no buffered instruction to feed decode. A small\n  sequential prefetch buffer is a structural way to recover IPC from those\n  stalls while leaving the proven EX/MUL datapath alone.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the purely combinational IF/ID feed with a two- or four-entry\n  sequential instruction skid FIFO. The fetch side keeps issuing the next\n  sequential PC whenever the FIFO is not full, including during dmem/divider\n  stalls that currently freeze fetch, and pushes returned instructions only\n  when io_imemReady is high. The decode side consumes one buffered instruction\n  whenever ID can accept it; if the FIFO is empty it presents an invalid\n  bubble just like today's imem stall behavior. Redirects flush the FIFO and\n  restart fetching at the resolved target, so this is not a branch predictor\n  and it preserves the existing RVFI order and trap behavior. The expected\n  win is higher CoreMark iterations/cycle by hiding isolated iStall cycles\n  behind already-buffered sequential instructions, with modest timing risk\n  because the FIFO control stays in the front end and avoids the EX ALU cone.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a small sequential instruction FIFO with independent fetch and decode sides, redirect flush, and fetch-ahead while downstream stages are stalled.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Replace raw imem-ready stalling with FIFO-empty/decode-valid handling, suppress load-use checks on invalid buffered entries, and allow fetch to continue during dmem stalls when space is available.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the revised front-end valid/consume/full signals between IF, ID, and hazard while preserving the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Keep the IF/ID payload format stable or add only minimal front-end metadata needed for buffered valid/PC/instruction entries.\"\n  - file: test/test_if_prefetch_fifo.py\n    description: \"Add focused cocotb coverage for imem stall hiding, redirect FIFO flush, dmem-stall fetch-ahead, and load-use bubbles with queued instructions.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
