{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_1", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'rg -n \"category: structural|structural|IF|ID|EX|MEM|WB|stall|hazard|forward|regfile|pipeline|stage|split|merge|retire|load|store|effective_addr|result rails\" cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261004-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Move DIV/REM off the single-cycle ALU path\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded timing result has a very deep worst path running from the\\npipeline registers through the forwarding muxes and into the execute ALU.\\nThe current RV32M ALU implements DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU with single-cycle\\nSystemVerilog \\\"/\\\" and \\\"%\\\" operators, forcing Gowin timing to close a full\\n32-bit divider/remainder path in one cycle even though CoreMark's timed loop\\nis dominated by loads, stores, branches, simple integer ops, and MUL.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded timing result has a very deep worst path running from the\\npipeline registers through the forwarding muxes and into the execute ALU.\\nThe current RV32M ALU implements DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU with single-cycle\\nSystemVerilog \\\"/\\\" and \\\"%\\\" operators, forcing Gowin timing to close a full\\n32-bit divider/remainder path in one cycle even though CoreMark's timed loop\\nis dominated by loads, stores, branches, simple integer ops, and MUL.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Keep the RV32I ALU and MUL/MULH variants single-cycle, but replace the\\ncombinational DIV/REM cases with a small iterative divide unit in execute.\\nWhen a DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU enters EX, freeze upstream pipeline state until the\\nquotient/remainder is ready, then let the instruction advance normally with\\nthe exact RV32M result and RVFI metadata. This removes the long divider and\\nmodulo logic from the cycle-time path scored by static timing, while the IPC\\ncost should be negligible for CoreMark if timed-region divides are rare.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 18, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove single-cycle DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operators from the combinational ALU and leave only RV32I plus single-cycle multiply results on the fast path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate/control an iterative divider for DIV/REM ops, hold the EX/MEM register while it runs, and mux its comple\n…[85672 of 88744 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d890daff59cd6591]…\nssion\", \"fitness\": 115.65, \"delta_pct\": -18.3, \"vs_baseline\": 854.21, \"fmax_mhz\": 51.79, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4478102, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3199, \"ff\": 989, \"seeds\": [50.174, 51.79, 51.79], \"perturbations\": [[0, 50.174, 20], [1, 51.79, 19], [2, 51.79, 19]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"cpu/ras0_q_20_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -14.93, \"arrival_ns\": 25.225, \"logic_cells\": 46, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 20, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T07:36:58.687114Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-04 hyp-20261004-003-r6s2 (regression, -18.30%): Even RET-only prediction can lose badly when `ret_pred_target`/`ret_pred_valid` are carried through IF/ID and ID/EX and checked against the EX JALR target, because CoreMark's return bubbles do not amortize the added fetch/control and repair-path logic.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
