rol metadata if needed so registered repair can squash the fall-through instruction before side effects.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Replace same-cycle EX redirect PC selection with a registered repair input, keeping normal pc+4 as the static not-taken predicted next PC.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Emit registered repair requests for taken branches and jumps, and accept an explicit kill input that turns a wrong-path instruction into a bubble before EX/MEM side effects.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Integrate the registered repair and wrong-path kill with existing load-use, dmem-stall, imem-stall, and divider-busy priorities without double retirement.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Add the repair-target and kill-token flops and wire them between EX, IF, hazard, and ID/EX while preserving the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_registered_repair_predictor.py\n    description: \"Cover taken and not-taken branches, JAL and JALR repair, wrong-path load/store squashing, and imem/dmem stalls around a pending registered redirect.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
