{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r11s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-003-r11s2\ntitle: \"Predict source use for load hazards\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior control-flow predictors for this core have consistently spent more timing\n  budget than they saved, because even tiny target predictors add logic to the\n  IF next-PC mux or the EX repair path.  The remaining predictor-shaped\n  opportunity is to avoid a recurring conservative pipeline bubble without\n  touching the PC path: the current load-use detector stalls on any rs1/rs2\n  match, even when the matching field is not actually consumed by the following\n  instruction.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a small decode-side source-use predictor/classifier that marks whether\n  the instruction in IF/ID will really consume rs1 and rs2 in EX.  Feed those\n  bits into the load-use hazard check so a load to the nominal rs2 field of an\n  I-type ALU op, load, JALR, or immediate shift does not create a false bubble,\n  and so rs fields in known no-source instructions such as LUI, AUIPC, JAL,\n  FENCE, and EBREAK are ignored.  Reserved or otherwise illegal encodings should\n  default to both sources used, matching the decoder's conservative default and\n  avoiding any weakening of RVFI source-data behavior on traps.  This should\n  improve CoreMark iterations/cycle by removing decode bubbles on common\n  immediate and control instructions while keeping the predictor off the IF\n  next-PC mux and away from the MUL/forwarding critical path that defeated\n  earlier branch predictors.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Qualify load-use comparisons with predicted rs1_used and rs2_used bits instead of blindly matching both encoded source fields.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Derive cheap rs1/rs2 use bits from the IF/ID opcode/funct fields in parallel with decode and expose them to the top-level hazard unit.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the decode-side source-use prediction bits into the hazard unit while preserving the existing nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_load_use_predictor.py\n    description: \"Cover false load-use cases such as load-to-ADDI rs2 bits and load-to-LUI/JAL fields, plus true load-use cases for branches, stores, JALR, and R-type ops.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
