{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r12s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-003-r12s2\ntitle: \"Tagged direct-control target predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The core still resolves all taken branches and jumps in EX, so recurring\n  CoreMark loop backedges and direct jumps pay front-end bubbles. Prior\n  predictors lost because they decoded branch immediates in IF, carried wide\n  target metadata through the pipe, or validated against the live fetch PC.\n  A learned direct-control target table can avoid the IF decode/add path by\n  reusing targets already computed in EX.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a very small tagged taken-target predictor for direct control flow\n  only, populated from EX when a conditional branch is taken or a JAL\n  redirects. IF performs only a PC-index/tag lookup and, on a hit, selects\n  the stored target as the next PC; otherwise it keeps the current static\n  not-taken PC+4 path. Carry only a compact prediction token plus the stored\n  target needed for age-aligned repair into EX, so EX can suppress redirects\n  on exact predicted-target matches and redirect to pc+4 or the resolved\n  target on not-taken/alias misses. Do not predict JALR/returns and do not\n  construct immediates in IF. This targets the hottest direct loop/control\n  penalties while avoiding the opcode predecode, return stack, and live\n  fetch-PC repair mechanisms that made earlier predictor attempts regress.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add compact predicted-taken/target metadata to IF/ID and ID/EX so EX can repair using the age-aligned prediction rather than the live fetch PC.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a tiny tagged taken-target table for direct branches/JALs, use hit targets for the fetch PC, and keep the miss path identical to PC+4.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Update the direct-control predictor from resolved EX targets, suppress redirects on exact predicted-target hits, and repair not-taken or wrong-target predictions.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire prediction metadata and update signals between IF and EX while preserving the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_direct_target_predictor.py\n    description: \"Cover predicted taken loops, direct JAL hits, not-taken retraining/repair, alias repair, and stalls around predicted control flow.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
