{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'rg -n \"hyp-20261004-003-r3s2|hyp-20261004-003-r4s2|hyp-20261004-003-r8s2|hyp-20261004-003-r9s2|hyp-20261004-003-r1s2|hyp-20261004-003-r5s2|hyp-20261004-003-r6s2|hyp-20261004-003-r7s2\" cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261004-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny BTB next-PC predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current five-stage core fetches the sequential PC until a branch or jump\\nresolves in EX, so every taken conditional branch and every jump pays a\\nfront-end flush penalty. CoreMark's timed region has hot loops, direct calls,\\nand repeated returns, making taken-control penalties a plausible IPC loss that\\ncan be attacked without touching the ALU critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current five-stage core fetches the sequential PC until a branch or jump\\nresolves in EX, so every taken conditional branch and every jump pays a\\nfront-end flush penalty. CoreMark's timed region has hot loops, direct calls,\\nand repeated returns, making taken-control penalties a plausible IPC loss that\\ncan be attacked without touching the ALU critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a small direct-mapped next-PC predictor in IF: a 16-entry BTB indexed by\\nfetch PC, with a modest tag, predicted target, and 2-bit taken counter. IF\\nuses a valid tag hit with a taken counter to fetch the predicted target;\\notherwise it fetches PC+4. EX computes the architectural next PC exactly as\\ntoday, compares it with the predicted next PC carried down the pipe, and only\\nredirects/flushes on a mismatch. Update the BTB in EX for conditional\\nbranches, JAL, and JALR; train conditional counters up/down and force jumps\\nstrongly taken. This should remove most recurring loop and call/return\\nredirects while adding only a small PC-indexed lookup outside the current\\nforwarding-to-ALU worst path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend IF/ID, ID/EX, and EX/MEM payloads with predicted next-PC metadata used for redirect verification and RVFI-safe propagation.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the 16-entry BTB/counter predictor, drive predicted next PC into the PC update path, and expose prediction metadata to decode.\"}, \n…[38822 of 41894 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:cf605fd99dfd1869]…\negression\", \"fitness\": 138.49, \"delta_pct\": -2.16, \"vs_baseline\": 1042.66, \"fmax_mhz\": 59.719, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4312067, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3116, \"ff\": 975, \"seeds\": [58.594, 59.719, 59.719], \"perturbations\": [[0, 58.594, 19], [1, 59.719, 17], [2, 59.719, 17]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_1_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs2_val_0_s95\", \"slack_ns\": -12.066, \"arrival_ns\": 22.361, \"logic_cells\": 47, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 19, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T08:23:28.615653Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 9, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-04 hyp-20261004-003-r9s2 (regression, -2.16%): Even with only a `predicted_taken` bit carried to EX, a one-entry loop predictor still pays IF-side branch decode, B-immediate fingerprint compare, and target mux cost that CoreMark back-edge bubble savings did not amortize.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
