{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r12s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-003-r12s2\ntitle: \"Verified direct-target memo predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The core still resolves all taken branches and jumps in EX, so recurring\n  CoreMark loop backedges and direct jumps pay front-end bubbles. Prior\n  predictors lost because they decoded branch immediates in IF, carried wide\n  target metadata through the pipe, or validated against the live fetch PC.\n  The closest miss was the one-bit learned loop predictor, but correctness\n  pressure pushed branch-immediate fingerprinting into IF. A verified target\n  memo can move that check out of the next-PC decision.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a one-entry or two-entry learned taken-target memo for direct control\n  flow only, populated from EX after an actually taken conditional branch or\n  direct JAL. Each entry stores the branch PC tag, resolved target, and the\n  full 32-bit instruction word that produced that target. IF predicts solely\n  from an exact PC-tag hit and muxes the stored target into the PC path; it\n  does not decode opcodes, reconstruct immediates, run counters, or compare\n  instruction fingerprints before choosing next PC.\n\n  The fetched instruction and stored instruction word are latched together\n  into ID/EX as a compact verified-prediction token: if they match, EX may\n  suppress the normal taken redirect when the conditional branch resolves\n  taken or the JAL resolves; if a predicted conditional branch resolves not\n  taken, EX repairs to pc+4. If the instruction word does not match, EX\n  treats the prediction as an alias and repairs to pc+4 while flushing the\n  speculatively fetched target. This keeps target lookup local to IF and\n  carries only a small token to EX, while preserving correctness for symbolic\n  or changing instruction streams without the IF-side B-immediate fingerprint\n  cost that hurt the prior one-bit loop predictor. Do not predict JALR or\n  returns.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add compact prediction metadata for PC-tag hits, instruction-word verification, alias repair, and predicted direct-control state.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add the tiny PC-tagged taken-target memo with stored instruction words, use hit targets for the fetch PC, and keep the miss path identical to PC+4.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the prediction token and verify the fetched instruction word against the memo word without feeding that comparison back into the same-cycle next-PC mux.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Update the memo from resolved direct control flow, suppress redirects only for verified predicted-taken branches/JALs, and repair loop exits or alias predictions to pc+4.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire prediction metadata and update signals between IF and EX while preserving the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_verified_target_predictor.py\n    description: \"Cover predicted taken loops, direct JAL hits, not-taken repairs, instruction-word alias repair, and imem/dmem stalls around predicted control flow.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
