{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r13s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-003-r13s2\ntitle: \"Hot loop replay predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior branch predictors regressed because they put target lookup, immediate\n  reconstruction, or wide prediction validation on the IF/ID/EX control path.\n  The tiny I-cache nearly cleared the acceptance bar by reducing frontend stall\n  cycles, but its per-fetch tag/data mux cost still hurt timing. CoreMark's\n  hottest work is loop dominated, so a predictor that only activates after a\n  learned backward loop and then streams by position may recover the same\n  frontend cycles with less global fetch cost.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a single hot-loop replay predictor in the fetch stage. Train it from EX\n  when a conditional branch resolves taken to a lower PC, storing loop_start,\n  loop_end, and a small valid/instruction array filled from normal imem fetches\n  while the loop body is observed. Once all words from loop_start through\n  loop_end are valid, a later fetch at loop_start enters replay mode: IF serves\n  instructions from the local array by a small sequential index, ignores\n  io_imemReady for those hits, and predicts the branch at loop_end taken by\n  wrapping the fetch PC back to loop_start.\n\n  EX still resolves the loop branch exactly. If the branch exits, or if any\n  redirect/jump leaves the learned range, replay mode is cancelled and the\n  existing redirect path repairs to the architectural PC. The miss path and all\n  non-loop control flow remain the current static not-taken design. This keeps\n  the common fetch path to one loop-active mux plus an entry equality check,\n  avoids BTB counters and predicted-target tokens, and targets both taken\n  backedge bubbles and the random imem stalls inside CoreMark hot loops.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add compact loop-replay metadata fields for replay hit, loop index, and predicted wrap state without carrying full predicted targets through the pipe.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Implement the single hot-loop replay predictor, fill the loop instruction array from normal fetches, serve replay hits locally, and wrap at the learned loop end.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Detect taken backward conditional branches for training, suppress correct predicted-wrap redirects, and cancel replay on loop exit or non-loop redirects.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire loop training, replay metadata, and effective instruction-ready status between IF, EX, and the existing hazard unit.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Use the fetch stage's effective instruction-ready signal so replayed loop-body instructions do not bubble when raw io_imemReady is low.\"\n  - file: test/test_loop_replay_predictor.py\n    description: \"Cover loop fill, replay during imem stalls, predicted backedge wrap, loop exit repair, redirects out of replay mode, and reset invalidation.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
