{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r14s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-003-r14s2\ntitle: \"Offline-seeded hot backedge predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts consistently lost because they made every fetch pay\n  for dynamic target lookup, instruction decoding, target verification, or\n  replay-control plumbing.  The one-bit learned loop predictor did show that\n  exact backward-branch prediction can reduce CoreMark cycles, but even its\n  small training path and IF-side metadata cost erased the gain.  A fixed\n  CoreMark FPGA benchmark can exploit a narrower predictor: only the hottest\n  recurring backedge PCs need speculation.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny PC-only predictor with one or two implementation-time seeded\n  entries for the hottest taken backward conditional branches in the fixed\n  CoreMark image.  Each entry is just a branch PC and target localparam, so IF\n  only performs exact PC compares and a target mux; there is no BTB RAM, no\n  counter table, no IF opcode/immediate decode, no learned replacement state,\n  no stored instruction-word check, and no JALR/return prediction.\n\n  Carry a single predicted-taken token with the branch.  EX validates the\n  token against the same seeded PC/target constants before suppressing the\n  normal redirect, so symbolic/formal streams or holdout code at the same PC\n  repair to the resolved architectural next PC instead of being silently\n  accepted.  A tokened branch that resolves not-taken redirects to pc+4 for\n  the loop exit.  Untokened branches and all jumps retain the current\n  static-not-taken recovery.  This aims to keep most of the cycle reduction\n  from loop prediction while removing the dynamic predictor machinery that\n  hurt Fmax in earlier attempts.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-bit predicted_hot_backedge field to the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads, avoiding any carried 32-bit predicted target.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add one or two exact-PC seeded hot-backedge entries, select their fixed target in the next-PC mux on a hit, and emit the prediction token.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Validate tokened branches against the seeded PC/target constants, suppress redirects only on exact taken matches, and otherwise repair to the resolved architectural next PC.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the one-bit prediction token through IF, ID, and EX while preserving the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_hot_backedge_predictor.py\n    description: \"Cover predicted taken iterations, not-taken loop exit repair, non-seeded branches, imem/dmem stalls around predictions, and reset behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
