{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r2s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-003-r2s2\ntitle: \"Table-free backward branch predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The existing core resolves every taken conditional branch in EX, so hot\n  CoreMark loops pay a front-end bubble on each taken back edge. A prior\n  16-entry BTB/counter predictor regressed badly because the table lookup and\n  predicted-PC plumbing inflated timing and area. The remaining predictor\n  opportunity is therefore a much cheaper static predictor that captures loop\n  behavior without any SRAM/LUTRAM state.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a table-free static backward-taken, forward-not-taken predictor for\n  conditional branches in IF. Decode only the BRANCH opcode and the sign of\n  its B-immediate; if the branch offset is negative, set the fetch PC to\n  pc+imm, otherwise keep pc+4. Carry the predicted next PC through ID/EX, and\n  have EX redirect only when the resolved architectural next PC differs from\n  that prediction. CoreMark's inner loops should avoid most taken-backedge\n  redirect bubbles, while the implementation avoids the BTB tags, counters,\n  and update path that hurt the prior predictor attempt.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a predicted-next-PC field to the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads so EX can validate the static prediction without changing RVFI retirement width.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Decode conditional-branch immediates in fetch and choose pc+imm only for negative-offset branches; keep existing redirect and stall priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the fetch-stage predicted next PC into ID/EX alongside the decoded instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute the resolved architectural next PC as today, compare it with the carried prediction, and redirect/flush only on mismatch or trap recovery.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the widened pipeline payloads through the existing single-issue datapath without altering the top-level IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_static_branch_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add focused cocotb coverage for repeated backward taken branches, loop exit mispredict recovery, and forward not-taken behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
