{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r7s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-003-r7s2\ntitle: \"Decode-stage backward branch predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts lost because they put target lookup, immediate\n  assembly, or wide predicted-PC validation on the fetch and execute timing\n  paths. The remaining useful branch opportunity is CoreMark's loop backedges,\n  but it needs to avoid an IF-stage BTB, counters, tag compares, and carried\n  32-bit predicted targets.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a decode-stage static backward-taken predictor for conditional branches.\n  ID already has the fetched instruction, PC, decoded opcode, and B-immediate,\n  so it can recognize a valid conditional branch with a negative immediate and\n  request the IF PC to take pc+imm one cycle before the current EX redirect.\n  Carry only a single predicted_taken bit with the branch into ID/EX.\n\n  EX still resolves the branch exactly. If the backward prediction was correct,\n  suppress the normal taken-branch redirect and keep the already-fetched target\n  instruction. If it was wrong, redirect to pc+4 and flush the target-path\n  instruction through the existing recovery path. Forward branches and all\n  jumps keep the current not-taken/EX-resolved behavior. This attacks hot loop\n  control bubbles while avoiding the failed predictor costs called out in the\n  lessons: no BTB, no IF immediate builder, no predictor RAM, and no 32-bit\n  predicted-target compare in EX.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-bit predicted_taken field to IF/ID and ID/EX branch metadata, cleared by existing bubbles and flushes.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Recognize valid conditional branches with negative B-immediates, compute pc+imm using the existing immediate, and emit a decode-stage predicted redirect plus the predicted_taken bit.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Accept a decode-stage predicted redirect target with lower priority than EX repair/redirect but higher priority than sequential pc+4, preserving stall behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Suppress the normal taken-branch redirect when predicted_taken matches the resolved taken result, and redirect to pc+4 on predicted-taken but actually-not-taken repair.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the decode prediction request/target and one-bit metadata between ID, IF, and EX without changing the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Treat decode prediction like a control redirect for wrong-path load-use masking and flush priority, while leaving dmem and divider holds intact.\"\n  - file: test/test_decode_branch_predictor.py\n    description: \"Cover correct backward-taken predictions, predicted-taken repairs to pc+4, forward branches staying unresolved until EX, and stalls coincident with prediction.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
