{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r8s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-003-r8s2\ntitle: \"Hit-bit loop target predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts show that CoreMark has enough recurring taken\n  control flow to save roughly four to five percent of cycles, but the usual\n  BTB/decode-predictor machinery loses more Fmax than it gains. The most\n  promising remaining predictor angle is to keep the target lookup local to\n  fetch and stop carrying wide predicted-target metadata through the pipe.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a two-entry learned taken-target memo for recurring backward\n  conditional branches. Each entry stores a valid bit, the fetch PC, and the\n  resolved target learned in EX after an actually-taken backward branch.\n  Fetch predicts only on an exact PC hit, selecting the stored target as the\n  next PC; otherwise it continues to use pc+4. The IF/ID and ID/EX bundles\n  carry only a one-bit prediction-hit marker.\n\n  In EX, compute the architectural next PC exactly as today. For a predicted\n  instruction, validate by comparing that resolved next PC with the current\n  fetch PC, which should be the predicted target when the prediction was\n  accepted. A match suppresses the normal taken-branch redirect; a mismatch\n  redirects to the resolved next PC and flushes normally. This keeps target\n  muxing local to IF, avoids IF opcode/immediate decode, avoids counters and\n  tag RAMs, and removes the full predicted-target field that hurt the earlier\n  loop and return predictors.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-bit prediction-hit field to IF/ID and ID/EX metadata, cleared by existing reset, flush, and bubble behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Implement a two-entry PC-tagged taken-target memo local to fetch and select the stored target only on an exact PC hit.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Train the memo from actually-taken backward branches, suppress redirects when the prediction matches the resolved next PC, and repair to the resolved next PC on misses.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire predictor hit, current fetch PC, and EX update signals between IF and EX without changing the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Treat prediction repair like the existing EX redirect for flush and load-use masking while preserving dmem and divider stall priority.\"\n  - file: test/test_hit_bit_loop_predictor.py\n    description: \"Cover predicted taken loop branches, loop exit repair to pc+4, stale-entry repair, and imem/dmem stall interactions.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
