{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r9s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-003-r9s2\ntitle: \"One-bit loop prediction token\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts show that CoreMark can save cycles on recurring\n  taken loop branches, but every design that carries a predicted target or\n  adds decode-to-fetch immediate logic has lost more Fmax than it recovers.\n  The latest hit-bit loop predictor had the right instinct, yet it validated\n  against the live fetch PC after fetch had already advanced, turning correct\n  predictions into repairs and a long IF/EX control loop.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a single-entry learned backward-branch target memo in IF. The entry\n  stores a valid bit, the branch PC tag, and the resolved target learned from\n  EX after an actually taken conditional branch with a backward target. Fetch\n  predicts only on an exact PC-tag hit and uses the stored target as next PC;\n  otherwise it keeps the current pc+4 behavior.\n\n  Carry only a one-bit predicted_taken token from IF/ID into ID/EX. EX does\n  not compare a carried 32-bit predicted target and does not look at the live\n  fetch PC. Instead, for conditional branches with predicted_taken set, an\n  actually taken result is accepted as correct because the exact PC-tagged\n  static instruction has a deterministic target; an actually not-taken result\n  redirects to pc+4 as the loop-exit repair. Unpredicted taken branches keep\n  the current EX redirect path and train or replace the memo. This should\n  recover hot back-edge bubbles while keeping predictor cost to one IF-local\n  tag compare, one target mux, one metadata bit, and no wide EX validation\n  path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a predicted_taken bit to IF/ID and ID/EX bundles so prediction age is aligned with the branch instruction and cleared by existing bubbles.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add the single-entry exact-PC backward-branch target memo, use it only for local next-PC selection, and emit the one-bit prediction token.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Train the memo from actually taken backward conditional branches, suppress redirects for predicted-taken branches that resolve taken, and repair loop exits to pc+4.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Pass the prediction token from IF/ID to ID/EX without adding decode-stage predictor logic.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire predictor update and one-bit metadata between IF, ID, and EX while preserving the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_loop_predictor.py\n    description: \"Cover taken-loop prediction, loop-exit repair, replacement by another backward branch, and imem or dmem stalls around predicted branches.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
